.TH RPL 1 "2026-07-09" "reta arch mojo" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
rpl \- start the compact logged Reta prompt profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpl
.RI [ prompt-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpl
starts a historical Reta prompt profile for compact interactive work.  Compared
with
.BR rp ,
it uses vi mode, starts with logging disabled and enables the compact
.B e
command behaviour by default.
.PP
It is useful when the prompt should print fewer explanatory lines while keeping
the same command language as
.BR rp .
.SH OPTIONS
.B rpl
accepts the same startup options as
.BR rp (1):
.BR -vi ,
.BR -log ,
.BR -language=LANGUAGE ,
.BR -debug ,
.BR -befehl ,
.B -e
and
.BR -h .
.SH COMMAND LANGUAGE
The interactive commands are the same as in
.BR rp (1).
Common commands include
.BR a ,
.BR u ,
.BR prim ,
.BR multis ,
.BR modulo ,
.BR reta ,
.BR shell ,
.BR python ,
.BR math ,
.BR S ,
.BR s ,
.B o
and
.BR l .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/rpl
Default public executable for a standard installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_interactive_mojo.so
Interactive prompt library used by
.BR rpl .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
rpl
rpl -befehl prim 60
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rp (1),
.BR rpe (1),
.BR rpb (1),
.BR reta (1)
